From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000006 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WLTB Gino <gino@wltb.local>
Subject: [PATCH] ingenic-sdk: gc4023 t41: add the real 30fps mode

The t41 port's win_sizes[0] claims "2560x1440 @max 30fps" but points at
the 25fps register table (VTS 0x0753 = 1875). Every T41 board with this
sensor therefore boots at 25fps no matter what the caps advertise, and
SENSOR_SUPPORT_30FPS_SCLK is computed from the never-shipped 30fps
table (2025*1200*2*25), so runtime fps requests derive garbage VTS
values from the bogus constant.

Port the true 30fps table from the t32 sibling (mipi 864Mbps/lane, PLL
0x0a36=0x60, 0x061d/e=0x22/0x78, VTS 0x05dc=1500), aim win_sizes[0] at
it, and restore the OTP/BLC/DPC init tail plus the 0x0709/0x0719 and
0x0704/06/16/08/18 MIPI tuning registers that the t32 table runs and
every other t41 mode keeps.

SCLK handling differs from t32: the t41 set_fps doubles HTS
(((hts << 8) + tmp) << 1) before dividing, t32 does not. With hts=1200
the effective divisor is 2400, so the runtime clocks are:

- 108e6 = 0x960 * 0x8ca * 20 (doubled HTS 2400 x 20fps VTS 2250),
  shared by case 0 (30fps boot, vts 1500), case 2 (20fps) and case 3
  (15fps, vts 3000).
- 121.5e6 = 0x960 * 0x7e9 * 25 (doubled HTS 2400 x 25fps VTS 2025)
  for case 1 (25fps_24Mmipi), which gets its own constant and its own
  set_fps case.

The mipi bus struct is split per window: sensor_mipi_linear stays 864
for win_sizes[0]; the new sensor_mipi_25fps_linear carries 702 for the
704Mbps/lane 25fps_24Mmipi window (win_sizes[1]). Boot attributes are
corrected per window: one_line_expr_in_us 22us for the 27MHz-mclk
modes, 20us for the 24MHz-mclk 25fps mode (line time 19.75us);
total_height/max-integration 1500, 2250, 3000 and 2025 to match each
table; boot exposure 0x5a0 (1440) fits the new 30fps VTS-1500 maximum.
sensor_set_fps now also updates the sensor max-exposure registers
0x0259/0x025a = vts-32, matching the t32 driver.

The now-unused 25fps_mipi table is removed and the stale /*vts =
1500*/ comment on 25fps_24Mmipi corrected (registers say 2025).

T41NQ boards with GC4023 (Noorio T110) now boot at 30fps and honor fps
changes.

Signed-off-by: WLTB Gino <gino@wltb.local>
